{"parentUuid":"e78b15d9-2af6-48de-b566-6d0dc1cf1c5e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01StNjKrxtfeye3V7fe8Q8c8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DhTArjytBtqEARNSa7Vsur","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT OR-Tools restart_period restart_algorithms parameters"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7187,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":203,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7187},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":203,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7187,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy7w3351oAGHfEkcHVi","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"69e56f93-ae61-45a9-b38f-68ed55f81ba4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:24.075Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e78b15d9-2af6-48de-b566-6d0dc1cf1c5e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WYhDzjpWpUPzKiE7sYxFv6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT solver restart strategy Luby geometric LBD Glucose 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reﬁning restarts strategies for SAT and UNSAT\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/articles/xxmain.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Ultra Rapid Restarts⋆ Shai Haim1 and Marijn Heule2\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~mheule/publications/rapid.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"On the Glucose SAT Solver Gilles Audemard\",\"url\":\"https://univ-artois.hal.science/hal-03299473/document\"},{\"title\":\"GLUCOSE: a solver that predicts learnt clauses quality | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/239919469_GLUCOSE_a_solver_that_predicts_learnt_clauses_quality\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Learning-Based Restart Policy for CDCL SAT Solvers | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-94144-8_6\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another SAT Solver Benchmarks | by Shuji Narazaki | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@shnarazk/yet-another-sat-solver-benchmarks-4a4d67d5f712\"},{\"title\":\"GlueMiniSat 2.2.5: A Fast SAT Solver with An Aggressive Acquiring Strategy of Glue Clauses | CiNii Research\",\"url\":\"https://cir.nii.ac.jp/crid/1390001204736828160\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 1 (2024) 1-37\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.10705\"},{\"title\":\"Explaining SAT Solving Using Causal Reasoning Jiong Yang #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.28/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.28.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Improving Glucose for Incremental SAT Solving with ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/articles/xmain.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about SAT solver restart strategies, particularly focusing on Luby, geometric, LBD, and Glucose:\n\n## Key Restart Strategies\n\nOriginally Luby restarts were heavily used because they represent a priori optimal strategy, however, most implementations switched to Glucose-style restarts, which are essentially a requirement for prevailing in the SAT Competition.\n\n### Luby Sequence\n\nThe Luby sequence is log optimal when the runtime distribution of the problems is unknown. Using Luby sequences solves many more benchmark instances compared to the original version using geometric restart strategy.\n\n### LBD-Based Restarts and Glucose\n\nLBD (Literal Block Distance) is a quality measure that has been proven to be very informative in practice to predict clauses usefulness. A restart strategy based on LBD has been introduced and implemented in the solver Glucose.\n\nIt was proposed to nest two series, a geometric one and a Luby, to ensure that restarts are guaranteed to increase and that fast restarts occur more often than in the geometric series.\n\n### Recent Research\n\nRestarts improve the quality of learnt clauses as measured by literal block distance (LBD), and more frequent restarts decrease the LBD of learnt clauses, which in turn improves solver performance.\n\nThe search results do not contain specific information focused on 2024-2025 developments in SAT solver restart strategies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ebb394f3-c1d3-4b8d-a641-dfd6306f1767","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:30.425Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e78b15d9-2af6-48de-b566-6d0dc1cf1c5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"69e56f93-ae61-45a9-b38f-68ed55f81ba4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DhTArjytBtqEARNSa7Vsur","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT OR-Tools restart_period restart_algorithms parameters\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"7.2. Restarting the search — or-tools User's Manual\",\"url\":\"https://acrogenesis.com/or-tools/documentation/user_manual/manual/metaheuristics/restart.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/restart.cc at master · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/sat/restart.cc\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Setting solver limits | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_tasks\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"}]\n\nI found relevant search results about CP-SAT restart parameters in OR-Tools. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nThe restart policy in CP-SAT uses parameters like `restart_period()`, `num_conflicts_before_strategy_changes()`, `restart_running_window_size()`, and `blocking_restart_window_size()`.\n\nOn each restart, the solver randomly chooses whether to use decay or no decay.\n\nThe solver periodically abandons the current search tree and starts over with a different variable ordering, which prevents getting trapped in unproductive regions of the search space.\n\nAlthough restarts sound wasteful, they're effective because the solver retains all learned clauses, ensuring restarting doesn't waste the work already done and can find solutions much faster.\n\nModern restart strategies in CP-SAT use geometric sequences, Luby sequences, or adaptive strategies that adjust restart frequency based on solver progress.\n\nThe most detailed technical information appears to be in the OR-Tools source code file `sat_parameters.proto` on GitHub, which defines the protocol buffer parameters for restart configuration. For specific parameter details and their default values, you may want to consult the official OR-Tools documentation or the source code directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"76acf8cf-e78e-4baf-aa27-09decc4dbe00","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:31.769Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"69e56f93-ae61-45a9-b38f-68ed55f81ba4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
