{"parentUuid":"0fc8a94e-032b-41c1-883c-8454ef0b6e7a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DGJHUFjC1bKNNC1k7epRxk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RvVdYuUGXu4kXK6idrVWjN","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/sat/restart.cc","prompt":"Extract the restart algorithms supported (Luby, geometric, LBD, etc.) and the relevant parameter names like restart_algorithms, restart_period, restart_running_window_size, blocking_restart_window_size, and their default values."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_read_input_tokens":20308,"output_tokens":265,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2773},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":265,"cache_read_input_tokens":20308,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2773,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy8pURXRoAb4bfgq9V3","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c18226d5-6a09-4d55-9797-1118ae315a9a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:38.823Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0fc8a94e-032b-41c1-883c-8454ef0b6e7a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YDZufCtn3Ke6La3ckmFk5k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"chronological backtracking CDCL SAT solver 2024 Maple Kissat\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Lazy Reimplication in Chronological Backtracking - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.9\"},{\"title\":\"Conflict-driven clause learning - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conflict-driven_clause_learning\"},{\"title\":\"Chronological Backtracking | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-94144-8_7\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Chronological Backtracking\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/325968980_Chronological_Backtracking\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2024-solvers.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Backing Backtracking?\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/MoehleBiere-SAT19.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Deep Cooperation of CDCL and Local Search for SAT (Extended Abstract)*\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2022/0734.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Improving CDCL SAT Solving using Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.14053\"},{\"title\":\"Designing New Phase Selection Heuristics Arijit Shaw and Kuldeep S. Meel\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~meel/Papers/sat20-sm.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Rethinking Clause Management for CDCL SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.20829\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about chronological backtracking in CDCL SAT solvers with connections to Maple and Kissat:\n\n## Chronological Backtracking in CDCL SAT Solvers (2024)\n\nChronological backtracking is an interesting SAT solving technique within CDCL reasoning, as it backtracks less aggressively upon conflicts. However, chronological backtracking is more difficult to maintain due to its weaker SAT solving invariants.\n\n### Recent 2024 Research\n\nA notable 2024 publication addresses this challenge: \"Lazy Reimplication in Chronological Backtracking\" was published at the 27th International Conference on Theory and Applications of Satisfiability Testing (SAT 2024), focusing on how to maintain chronological backtracking more effectively.\n\n### Maple and Chronological Backtracking\n\nChronological backtracking improves the performance of the winner of the latest SAT Competition, Maple_LCM_Dist. The SAT solver Maple LCM Dist ChronoBT was ranked first in the main track of the SAT Competition 2018.\n\n### Kissat\n\nKissat series represents the state-of-the-art, having dominated the main track of the SAT Competitions from 2020 to 2025. While the search results don't specifically mention Kissat implementing chronological backtracking, they do indicate it's a leading modern CDCL solver that continues to be developed and improved.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"791a71ed-259d-4d41-a6dd-d7958ee5349d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:43.802Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0fc8a94e-032b-41c1-883c-8454ef0b6e7a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c18226d5-6a09-4d55-9797-1118ae315a9a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RvVdYuUGXu4kXK6idrVWjN","type":"tool_result","content":"# Restart Algorithms and Parameters in OR-Tools\n\nBased on the `restart.cc` file, the following restart algorithms are supported:\n\n**Supported Restart Algorithms:**\n1. `NO_RESTART` - No restart strategy\n2. `LUBY_RESTART` - Uses Luby sequence for restart intervals\n3. `DL_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART` - Restarts based on decision level moving averages\n4. `LBD_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART` - Restarts based on LBD (literal block distance) moving averages\n5. `FIXED_RESTART` - Fixed interval restarts\n\n**Key Parameter Names Referenced:**\n\n- `restart_algorithms` - Specifies which algorithms to cycle through\n- `default_restart_algorithms` - Default algorithm selection as comma-separated string\n- `restart_period` - Base period for restart intervals\n- `restart_running_window_size` - Window size for computing moving averages\n- `blocking_restart_window_size` - Window size for blocking restart logic\n- `restart_dl_average_ratio` - Threshold ratio for decision level averaging\n- `restart_lbd_average_ratio` - Threshold ratio for LBD averaging\n- `strategy_change_increase_ratio` - Growth factor when switching strategies\n- `blocking_restart_multiplier` - Multiplier for blocking restart conditions\n- `use_blocking_restart` - Boolean flag enabling blocking restart feature\n- `num_conflicts_before_strategy_changes` - Conflict count before strategy switches\n\n**Default Behavior:** When no algorithms are specified, the system defaults to `NO_RESTART`."}]},"uuid":"0a0d1498-9525-4b4e-ad23-338d2ebc0291","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:44.116Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c18226d5-6a09-4d55-9797-1118ae315a9a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0a0d1498-9525-4b4e-ad23-338d2ebc0291","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JKfRH6dTkVnbCCzx5rbPbY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DtQkzHwD66NBhyxn5UPWk4","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto","prompt":"Find the default values and documentation for: restart_algorithms, default_restart_algorithms, restart_period, restart_running_window_size, blocking_restart_window_size, restart_dl_average_ratio, restart_lbd_average_ratio, use_blocking_restart, num_conflicts_before_strategy_changes. Also report the default cycle of restart algorithms used."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2106,"cache_read_input_tokens":23081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2106,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":64,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy9jaXQJepTCZ6tG1ZH","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"58c6fb52-3792-45ce-aef7-9ab44190d5d3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:48.514Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"58c6fb52-3792-45ce-aef7-9ab44190d5d3","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JKfRH6dTkVnbCCzx5rbPbY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PCyMfG7YGcVeYukmrRdmtt","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"SAT competition 2025 winner restart strategy long unsatisfiable proof"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2106,"cache_read_input_tokens":23081,"output_tokens":313,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2106},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":313,"cache_read_input_tokens":23081,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2106,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy9jaXQJepTCZ6tG1ZH","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"19dff9b7-4e36-4844-ba7f-251f791d5806","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:49.059Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"58c6fb52-3792-45ce-aef7-9ab44190d5d3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DtQkzHwD66NBhyxn5UPWk4","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Solver Restart Algorithm Parameters\n\nBased on the `sat_parameters.proto` file, here are the key restart-related parameters:\n\n## Default Values\n\n| Parameter | Default |\n|-----------|---------|\n| `restart_algorithms` | (empty, uses `default_restart_algorithms`) |\n| `default_restart_algorithms` | \"LUBY_RESTART,LBD_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART,DL_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART\" |\n| `restart_period` | 50 |\n| `restart_running_window_size` | 50 |\n| `restart_dl_average_ratio` | 1.0 |\n| `restart_lbd_average_ratio` | 1.0 |\n| `use_blocking_restart` | false |\n| `blocking_restart_window_size` | 5000 |\n| `num_conflicts_before_strategy_changes` | 0 |\n\n## Default Restart Cycle\n\nThe solver employs a three-strategy portfolio that rotates: **Luby restart**, followed by **LBD-based moving average restart**, then **decision-level moving average restart**. These strategies cycle according to conflict counts and strategy-change thresholds.\n\n## Key Documentation\n\nThe moving average restart strategies trigger when window-averaged metrics exceed global averages by the specified ratios. Blocking restart prevents restarts when conflict trail sizes remain elevated, using a 5000-conflict window and 1.4× multiplier threshold by default."}]},"uuid":"b86e9bf9-ba33-4270-bb47-806b531cab5d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:52.869Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"58c6fb52-3792-45ce-aef7-9ab44190d5d3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"19dff9b7-4e36-4844-ba7f-251f791d5806","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PCyMfG7YGcVeYukmrRdmtt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT competition 2025 winner restart strategy long unsatisfiable proof\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competitions\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Refining Restarts Strategies for SAT and UNSAT | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-33558-7_11\"},{\"title\":\"Recent news about SAT for tag Competition\",\"url\":\"http://www.satlive.org/competition.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2020 - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0004370221001235\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/\"},{\"title\":\"The SAT Competition - CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/competitions.html\"},{\"title\":\"CanSat Competition\",\"url\":\"https://cansatcompetition.com/winners.html\"}]\n\nLet me search more specifically for the SAT Competition 2025 winner and details about unsatisfiable proofs:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GaloisSAT: Differentiable Boolean Satisfiability Solving via Finite Field Algebra\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2603.28796\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"KIT - SAtRes - MallobSat scores 1st in SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/news/2025-08-15-satcomp/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/certificates.html\"},{\"title\":\"SATLUTION: Autonomous SAT Solver Evolution\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/papers/2509.07367\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Modern SAT Solver With Machine Learning Method | Proceedings of the Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3716368.3735251\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2020 - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0004370221001235\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/output.html\"},{\"title\":\"SATLIB - Benchmark Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~hoos/SATLIB/benchm.html\"}]\n\nLet me search more specifically for MallobSat and restart strategies:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing - SAtRes\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2024-jair-mallobsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The resolution proof system — CS-E3220: Propositional satisfiability and SAT solvers documentation\",\"url\":\"https://users.aalto.fi/~tjunttil/2020-DP-AUT/notes-sat/resolution.html\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-jair-mallobsat-pre.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol341-sat2025/html/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27.html\"},{\"title\":\"KIT - SAtRes - MallobSat scores 1st in SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/news/2025-08-15-satcomp/\"},{\"title\":\"Proof Traces for SAT solvers | Wonderings of a SAT geek\",\"url\":\"https://www.msoos.org/2022/04/proof-traces-for-sat-solvers/\"},{\"title\":\"Decision Procedures and SAT/SMT Solvers NAIL094 Petr Kučera Charles University\",\"url\":\"http://ktiml.mff.cuni.cz/~kucerap/satsmt/presentation/satsmt-03.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Computing Small Unsatisfiable Cores in Satisfiability ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1401.3878\"},{\"title\":\"Proofs for Satisﬁability Problems Marijn J.H. Heule1 and Armin Biere2\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.utexas.edu/~marijn/publications/APPA.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Unsatisfiable core - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unsatisfiable_core\"}]\n\nLet me search more specifically for restart strategies and long unsatisfiable proofs:\n\nNo links found.\n\nBased on my web search results, I can provide you with information about the SAT Competition 2025 winner and some context about restart strategies in SAT solving:\n\n## SAT Competition 2025 Winner\n\nMallobSat scored the best on unsatisfiable instances and the 2nd best on satisfiable instances, overall resulting in a 1st place by a rather small margin (3% to Painless-PRS-Kissat in terms of the PAR-2 evaluation metric). 2025 marked the first year where their system was able to win the SAT competition's shared-memory parallel main track (64 threads).\n\n## Restart Strategies and Unsatisfiable Proofs\n\nRegarding restart strategies in SAT solving, the research shows an important relationship with proving unsatisfiability. Unsatisfiable formulas can miss a short proof of unsatisfiability with certain restart strategies, which restart after a specific number of conflicts with intervals between restarts that must increase over time.\n\nProving a formula's unsatisfiability requires a network of clausal dependencies, and all clauses along a critical path through this network need to be derived sequentially. This sequential nature of unsatisfiability proofs makes restart strategies particularly important—frequent restarts could disrupt the derivation of long chains of clauses needed for the proof.\n\nUnfortunately, the specific details about restart strategies used by MallobSat for handling long unsatisfiable proofs were not fully covered in the search results I found.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"56748c65-8bd9-4d0a-b4e9-67fce77d5cb5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:01.626Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"19dff9b7-4e36-4844-ba7f-251f791d5806","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"56748c65-8bd9-4d0a-b4e9-67fce77d5cb5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1383ccced788ce49","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SGwCRJGb92bwg2nHNTUThm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me consolidate.\n\n---\n\n## SAT Solver Restart 策略调研（2024-2026）\n\n### 1. 经典 restart 策略对比\n\n| 策略 | 触发方式 | 适合场景 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Fixed**（固定周期） | 每 N 个 conflict 重启一次 | 教学；现代求解器基本不用 |\n| **Geometric**（MiniSat 风格） | N, N·r, N·r², ...（r≈1.5） | 早期 MiniSat；UNSAT 友好（间隔越拉越长，能完成长证明链） |\n| **Luby**（1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 4, ...） | Luby 序列 × unit | 运行时间分布未知时**对数最优**；SAT-leaning 短跑友好 |\n| **LBD-based**（Glucose）| 当短窗 LBD 均值 > 全局均值 × K 时重启 | SAT-leaning 现代主流，但**对 UNSAT 长证明不友好** |\n| **DL moving average** | 决策层均值飙升时重启 | 跟 LBD 互补，CP-SAT 默认开 |\n\n要点：UNSAT 证明本质是**有向 clause 依赖链**——需要按顺序推导所有 critical clause。**重启太频繁会反复打断这条链**，让 proof 永远长不出来。SAT 短跑则相反，频繁重启能跳出陷阱。\n\n### 2. Glucose 的 LBD-based restart\n\n- **核心指标**：LBD（Literal Block Distance，学习子句涉及的不同决策层数量），LBD 越低 = clause 越\"通用\" = 价值越高\n- **Forcing restart**：短窗（默认 50 个 conflict）平均 LBD 比全局平均 LBD 高出 K 倍 → 立即重启（说明最近学的 clause 质量差）\n- **Blocking restart**：当 trail size 在长窗（5000 conflict）内显著高于均值（×1.4）→ **抑制重启**（说明快出解了，别打断）\n- 对 UNSAT 的妥协：Glucose 论文（Audemard & Simon）专门提到这种激进重启**会拖慢 UNSAT**，所以引入 blocking restart 部分缓解\n\n### 3. Chronological Backtracking (CDCL-CB)\n\n- **原理**：传统 CDCL 冲突回溯到 \"asserting level\"（可能跳很多层）；CB 只回溯**一层**，保留更多 trail 状态\n- **历史**：Möhle & Biere（SAT'18 \"Backing Backtracking?\"）首次系统化；Maple_LCM_Dist_ChronoBT 拿了 SAT'18 冠军\n- **2024 进展**：SAT'24 \"Lazy Reimplication in Chronological Backtracking\" 解决了 CB 下传播不变量难维护的问题\n- **与 restart 的关系**：CB 让重启效益降低（trail 信息更值钱，丢了更可惜），现代 Kissat/CaDiCaL 倾向**减少重启 + 启用 CB**\n- **CP-SAT 现状**：未直接暴露 CB 开关，CP-SAT 走自己的 LP/CP 混合路线\n\n### 4. CP-SAT restart 相关参数（默认值来自 OR-Tools `sat_parameters.proto`）\n\n| 参数 | 默认值 | 含义 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `default_restart_algorithms` | `LUBY_RESTART,LBD_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART,DL_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART` | 三策略**轮换**（不是单选） |\n| `restart_period` | 50 | Luby 单位长度 + 短窗大小 |\n| `restart_running_window_size` | 50 | LBD/DL 短窗大小 |\n| `restart_lbd_average_ratio` | 1.0 | 短窗 LBD ≥ 全局 × 1.0 → 触发重启 |\n| `restart_dl_average_ratio` | 1.0 | DL 同上 |\n| `use_blocking_restart` | **false** | 默认**没开** Glucose blocking restart |\n| `blocking_restart_window_size` | 5000 | 一旦开启，长窗大小 |\n| `blocking_restart_multiplier` | 1.4 | 抑制重启的阈值倍数 |\n| `num_conflicts_before_strategy_changes` | 0 | 几次冲突后切换策略 |\n\n可选枚举：`NO_RESTART / LUBY_RESTART / DL_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART / LBD_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART / FIXED_RESTART`。\n\n### 5. 长跑场景下哪个最优\n\n研究共识 + SAT'25 经验（MallobSat 在 UNSAT 赛道夺冠）：\n- **SAT-leaning 短跑**：LBD-based + blocking，配 Luby 头几轮\n- **UNSAT-leaning 长跑**：**减少重启频率** + **开 blocking restart** + **延长 LBD/DL ratio 阈值**（>1.0 让重启更难触发）+ 配合 chronological backtracking\n- **未知**：默认三策略轮换（CP-SAT 现行做法）是对冲方案，长跑下偏 SAT 一些\n\n---\n\n## 我们硬候选 INFEASIBLE 证明的 restart 推荐配置\n\n硬候选 168h 长跑要证 UNSAT，不是搜 SAT 解，必须**抑制激进重启**让 conflict 链能完整长出来：\n\n```python\n# CP-SAT 参数推荐（Phase 3B Repair5 硬候选 INFEASIBLE 证明专用）\nsolver.parameters.restart_algorithms[:] = [\n    \"LUBY_RESTART\",                  # 保留对数最优兜底\n    \"LBD_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART\",    # 留一个 LBD，但调高阈值\n]\n# 关键：拉长重启周期，让长证明链不被打断\nsolver.parameters.restart_period = 200                  # 默认 50 → 4×\nsolver.parameters.restart_running_window_size = 200     # 短窗放宽\nsolver.parameters.restart_lbd_average_ratio = 1.4       # 默认 1.0 → 更难触发\nsolver.parameters.restart_dl_average_ratio = 1.4\n\n# 关键：开启 blocking restart（CP-SAT 默认 false！）\nsolver.parameters.use_blocking_restart = True\nsolver.parameters.blocking_restart_window_size = 5000\nsolver.parameters.blocking_restart_multiplier = 1.4\n\n# 长跑稳定性：策略切换不要太早\nsolver.parameters.num_conflicts_before_strategy_changes = 100000\n```\n\n**对照基线**：建议 A/B 对比三组（默认三策略 / 上面这套保守组 / `NO_RESTART` 极端组）跑 4-8h 取早期 conflict-rate 与 LBD 趋势，再决定 168h 用哪套。**不要**直接上 `NO_RESTART`——若早期分支选错，没重启就死循环。\n\nSources:\n- [On the Glucose SAT Solver — Audemard & Simon](https://univ-artois.hal.science/hal-03299473/document)\n- [Refining Restarts Strategies for SAT and UNSAT](http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/articles/xxmain.pdf)\n- [Towards Ultra Rapid Restarts — Haim & Heule](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~mheule/publications/rapid.pdf)\n- [Chronological Backtracking — Möhle & Biere SAT'18](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/MoehleBiere-SAT19.pdf)\n- [Lazy Reimplication in Chronological Backtracking — SAT'24](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.9)\n- [CaDiCaL/Kissat SAT Competition 2024 entry](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2024-solvers.pdf)\n- [MallobSat — SAT Competition 2025 winner (KIT news)](https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/news/2025-08-15-satcomp/)\n- [SAT Competition 2025 results slides](https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf)\n- [OR-Tools `restart.cc` source](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/sat/restart.cc)\n- [OR-Tools `sat_parameters.proto`](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [CP-SAT Primer — Parameters](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3231,"cache_read_input_tokens":25187,"output_tokens":3150,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3231},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3150,"cache_read_input_tokens":25187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3231,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyB2K86fK1sKof6miqX","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a9aa88c3-cf4c-44a8-95a5-62de04dae397","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:0